# apps/ios-shell/MyKhayaWidgets/ is a working copy `rsync -a --delete`d from
# native/widgets/ every time scripts/install-widget-sources.sh runs (part of
# the normal mac-bootstrap.sh flow, not just recovery) — the committed
# ios/App/App.xcodeproj references it via relative (../../MyKhayaWidgets/...)
# paths, but its actual Swift file contents are always a disposable, fully
# reproducible copy of the tracked apps/ios-shell/native/widgets/ source.
# Committing it would duplicate tracked source and risk it silently
# diverging from native/widgets/ if someone ever hand-edits the copy instead
# of the source. Same pattern as ios/App/App/public/ (Capacitor's own
# gitignore already excludes that regenerated copy for the same reason).
MyKhayaWidgets/
